"FreeDOS{"_N_
  "If you use FreeDOS/DOS from an USB then keep in mind,"_N_
  "that USB sticks may (relatively fast) wear out and get"_N_
  "slow when using them too much (write cycles)."_N_
  ""_N_
  "Please use a good DPMI host like hdpmi from the newest SBEMU"_N_
  "The program is very memory hungry. HDPMI32I.EXE provides"_N_
  "more than 1GB I think, maybe even 4GB."_N_
  ""_N_
  "The program is designed for DOS computers but for very fast"_N_
  "DOS computers. Maybe it is not a good idea to use it on e.g."_N_
  "a Pentium 200. The main reason is the resolution of"_N_
  "1024x768 used."_N_
  ""_N_
  "The program maybe used with old CRT monitors or even 16:9"_N_
  "monitors which are currently a standard as of 2026. There is"_N_
  "a setting in the menubar for it."_N_
"}"_N_
"Menubar{"_N_
  "The menubar is at the top of the screen."_N_
  "You can choose between different categories there."_N_
  "And do some settings, too."_N_
  "It also displays the current date and time."_N_
  "File{"_N_
    "In this menupoint there are file related operations."_N_
    "New image{"_N_
      "Let's you create a new image"_N_
      "The image gets inserted into pictures (in the menubar)"_N_
      "as last element and made as the current picture to edit."_N_
      "You can specify the width and the height"_N_
      "for the picture in pixels,centimeters or inch."_N_
      "For centimeters and inches there is a dpi"_N_
      "(dots per inch (or pixels per inch)) setting."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Load wyp image{"_N_
      "Let's you load a Wypa .wyp image. You can use the preview"_N_
      "function to see what you will be loading."_N_
      "The image is load with all it's layers."_N_
      "If you specify a non .wyp image, it get's also load but as"_N_
      "single layer."_N_
      "The image gets inserted into pictures (in the menubar)"_N_
      "as last element and made as the current picture to edit."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Save wyp image{"_N_
      "Let's you save the Wypa .wyp image you are currently"_N_
      "editing."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Import image{"_N_
      "If you load a Wypa .wyp image with this it gets 'reduced'"_N_
      "to a single layer."_N_
      "This option is for loading other formats than .wyp"_N_
      "and use them only as a (pseudo) single layer image at loading."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert image layers{"_N_
      "Inserts all the layers from another Wypa .wyp file"_N_
      "on top of the upperst currently selected layer."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert psd layers{"_N_
      "This option tries to import a Photoshop .psd file"_N_
      "with all it's layers on top of the upperst currently selected"_N_
      "layer."_N_
      "It is a very simple implementation and e.g. doesn't convert"_N_
      "the transparency modes of the layers."_N_
      "Maybe you should not rely on the 100% correctness of the"_N_
      "functionality of this feature."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert svg layer{"_N_
      "You can insert a vector graphic .svg file into the image here."_N_
      "It is imported as pixel graphic and not as vector graphic."_N_
      "But you may specify an alternative scaling for this pixel"_N_
      "graphic. E.g. a scale of 2 makes it double the size/resolution."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Export png{"_N_
      "Saves the complete image as single png file. It merges the layers"_N_
      "into this exported format."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Export layer(s) as single png {"_N_
      "Saves the selected layers as single png file. It merges the layers"_N_
      "into this exported format."_N_
    "}"_N_    
    "Export layer(s) as multiple pngs {"_N_
      "Saves the selected layers as multiple png files. With the layer"_N_
      "number inserted into the filename. You can specify if you want to"_N_
      "apply the post processing or save them in their raw format as png."_N_
    "}"_N_
  "}"_N_
  "Edit{"_N_
    "Undo{"_N_
      "Does a undo of the last operations."_N_
      "This function is not working for all/any of the changes"_N_
      "It actually should just help if you paint in the image"_N_
      "but many many other operations also feature an undo."_N_
      "You can see the number of available undos as [x] in"_N_
      "the undo options menu point."_N_
      "Maybe it is a good idea to save more often."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Redo{"_N_
      "Reverses the last made undos again."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Fill selection with color{"_N_
      "Fills the entire selected area of a layer(s) with the current"_N_
      "paint color."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Fill selection with alpha{"_N_
      "Fills the entire selected area of a layer(s) with the current"_N_
      "paint colors alpha(transparency)."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Erase selection{"_N_
      "Deletes the selected area of an layer."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Antialias selected{"_N_
      "Uses the called FXAA onto the selected area."_N_
      "FXAA is a anti aliasing and thus makes the structures"_N_
      "more smooth. FXAA is also called \"screen space antialiasing\"."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Greyscale{"_N_
      "Makes the selected area (or the whole area if nothing is"_N_
      "selected) from colored to grey. There is no luminance conversion"_N_
      "involved. This means you just get (red+green+blue)/3.\n"_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Gradiation curves{"_N_
      "This is for advanced users."_N_
      "It is possible to assign every color channel intensity"_N_
      "a new intensity by drawing curves."_N_
      "There is also a grey channel to adjust all the curves"_N_
      "at once. However if you use the grey channel in connection"_N_
      "with the red,green and blue updates it may introduce"_N_
      "problems when the colors are clipped from 0..255."_N_
      "So to say it doesn't stay just brighter/darker (visibly) in this"_N_
      "case it may get a color then. But it's at least already visible."_N_
      "This doesn't happen when you just use red/green/blue."_N_
      "You can save and load curves here."_N_
      "The CV option let's you edit Bezier handles. So you have real"_N_
      "curves instead of just linear changes."_N_
      "You may also enter the x and y position of the handles"_N_
      "directly."_N_
      "Every x position gets remapped to a y position (intensity)."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Color balance{"_N_
      "You can change the colorings of the image here."_N_
      "There is a option for the dark,middle and light part."_N_
      "Use the three sliders to adjust the colors of these."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Invert color{"_N_
      "Inverts the selected area (or the whole area if nothing is"_N_
      "selected) by using red = 255-red, green = 255-green,"_N_
      "blue = 255-blue."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Invert alpha{"_N_
      "Inverts the selected area (or the whole area if nothing is"_N_
      " selected) by using alpha(transparency) = 255-alpha."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Undo enabled{"_N_
      "You may disable undo. Undo uses rather much memory and is"_N_
      "not available for any operation in Wypa."_N_
    "}"_N_
  "}"_N_
  "Image{"_N_
    "Mirror horizontally{"_N_
      "Mirrors the entire image on it's x axis."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Mirror vertically{"_N_
      "Mirrors the entire image on it's y axis."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Rotate +90 degrees{"_N_
      "Rotates the entire image by 90degrees forward."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Rotate -90 degrees{"_N_
      "Rotates the entire image by 90degrees backward."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Fit canvas to layers{"_N_
      "Takes all the layers and makes the canvas/picture"_N_
      "as a picture that encompasses all (width/height)."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Crop canvas by alpha {"_N_
      "Takes all the active layers and makes the canvas/picture"_N_
      "as a picture that encompasses all (width/height). But"_N_
      "uses the alpha channel to determine whats visible (alpha!=0)."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Image properties{"_N_
      "You can specify the canvas width,height,x and y position."_N_
      "The canvas width and height is the size of the final picture"_N_
      "when exported."_N_
      "If you change the width or height you can use a 9x9 button"_N_
      "matrix to specify from which old canvas position changes apply"_N_
      "there is an instant preview for this visible in the background."_N_
      "Also you can change the grid cell width/height and x/y position."_N_
      "The grid is visible if you turn on the grid via the menu point"_N_
      "\"View\"->\"Show grid\""_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Resize image{"_N_
      "Maybe it's a good idea to save before resizing."_N_
      "Scales the current image to a new width/height."_N_
      "When quantization/baking is enabled all layers get"_N_
      "baked, thus you may loose pixel information, but the layers"_N_
      "get interpolated."_N_
      "You may specify \"Keep proportions\" to have the width/height"_N_
      "setting updated as you modify the other (width/height)setting."_N_
      "Interpolation modes:"_N_
      "Nearest pixel - just pixelated, keeps the color values the same."_N_
      "Linear - Modifies the color values but is smoother when zooming."_N_
      "Inter area - Modifies the color values on minification (smoothing)."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Fit canvas to selection{"_N_
      "Takes all the selections and fits the canvas to it."_N_
      "You get a picture that fits your selection (width/height)."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Duplicate picture{"_N_
      "Copies the picture with all its layers."_N_
      "The copied picture can be accessed with the menu point"_N_
      "\"Pictures\"."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Duplicate picture (merged){"_N_
      "Copies the picture merged down to a single layer."_N_
      "The copied picture can be accessed with the menu point"_N_
      "\"Pictures\"."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
  "}"_N_
  "Layer{"_N_
    "Add layer{"_N_
      "Inserts a bitmap layer above the first selected one."_N_
      "You can specify a width and height in pixels."_N_
      "It get's initially placed on the current pictures origin."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert layer like this layer{"_N_
      "Inserts a bitmap layer above the first selected one."_N_
      "It get's position and size and so on from the current layer."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Delete layer(s){"_N_
      "Deletes the selected layers."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert text layer{"_N_
      "Inserts an empty text layer above the first selected layer."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert adjustment layer{"_N_
      "Inserts an adjustment layer above the first selected layer."_N_
      "It has the size and position of the current canvas/image."_N_
      "Adjustment layers may be used to correct the colors of"_N_
      "underlying layers."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert tilemap layer with this layers tiles{"_N_
      "Inserts a tilemap layer above the first selected layer."_N_
      "It uses the current selected layer as tileset."_N_
      "Tilmaps can be used to draw levels for games."_N_
      "You can specify a x and y resolution of the tilemap."_N_
      "The tilemap is placed at the picture/canvas origin."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Hide all layers{"_N_
      "Turns off the visibility of all layers."_N_
      "You may turn then on individually then."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Show all layers{"_N_
      "Turns on the visibility of all layers."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Select all layers{"_N_
      "Selects all layers (but not their contents)."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Duplicate layer(s){"_N_
      "Duplicates of the selected layer(s) are placed above the layer(s)."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Copy layer(s){"_N_
      "Creates a merge of the current selected stuff/layer(s)."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Paste{"_N_
      "Pastes the merge of the current copied stuff/layer(s)."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Bake layer(s){"_N_
      "Layers are baked into a rectified form."_N_
      "Meaning: you get layer(s) without rotation or scaling."_N_
      "the pixels just are the pixels that you see in the final"_N_
      "image. Be careful here, since you lose information by that."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Merge down layer(s){"_N_
      "Layers are baked+merged to the bottom layer in a rectified form."_N_
      "Meaning: you get a layer without rotation or scaling."_N_
      "the pixels just are the pixels that you see in the final"_N_
      "image. Be careful here, since you lose information by that."_N_
      "All source layers are deleted by this."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert merge of layer(s){"_N_
      "Layers are baked+merged to the bottom layer in a rectified form."_N_
      "Meaning: you get a layer without rotation or scaling."_N_
      "the pixels just are the pixels that you see in the final"_N_
      "image. Be careful here, since you lose information by that."_N_
      "The source layers are kept but the merged layer is"_N_
      "placed above the first selected layer."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert alpha mask above layer(s){"_N_
      "All the selected layers are converted into an alphamask."_N_
      "Meaning: They get a grey value corresponding to their"_N_
      "transparency level."_N_
      "The converted layer(s) are inserted above the original layer(s)."_N_
      "The old layer(s) are kept."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Apply alpha mask to below{"_N_
      "The selected layers are combined (and deleted) with the layer(s)"_N_
      "below. The layer(s) below receive the grey (red+green+blue)/3"_N_
      "value as their new alpha channel (transparency) value."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Convert layer(s) from alpha to premul{"_N_
      "Most pictures you may find are not premultiplied alpha."_N_
      "So when you load them, there are colors visible in transparent"_N_
      "areas where they shouldn't. With this option you can convert"_N_
      "a normal alpha blending (normal) picture into the premul"_N_
      "mode."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Quantized palette from layer{"_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Quantize layer(s) to palette {"_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Mirror horizontally{"_N_
      "Mirrors layer(s) on the x axis."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Mirror vertically{"_N_
      "Mirror the layer(s) on the y axis."_N_
      "No undo."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Rotate +90 degrees{"_N_
      "Rotate the layer(s) by 90degrees forward."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Rotate -90 degrees{"_N_
      "Rotate the layer(s) by 90degrees backward."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Layer properties{"_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Crop layer(s) by alpha{"_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Lock layer(s){"_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Unlock layer(s){"_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Duplicate layer as reference{"_N_
    "}"_N_
  "}"_N_
  "Selection{"_N_
    "Selections are per layer. So to say if you select something on a"_N_
    "layer the selections stays only on that layer if you switch the"_N_
    "layer. You can press CTRL whilst switching the layer to copy"_N_
    "the selection."_N_
    "Select all{"_N_
      "Selects the entire layer region of the selected layer(s)."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Select none{"_N_
      "Removes the selection from all the layer(s)."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Invert selection{"_N_
      "Makes the selected pixels unselected and the non selected pixels"_N_
      "selected. On all selected layers."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Expand/shrink selection{"_N_
      "Expand or shrink the selection by an amount of pixels."_N_
      "This operation is slow if a big value is specified here."_N_
      "There is a button to switch from the default mode (expanding) to"_N_
      "shrinking."_N_
      "Thus the selection gets bigger or smaller by that."_N_
      "This operation works on all the selected layers."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Select by alpha{"_N_
      "The selection is created by all pixels >= a value and <= a value."_N_
      "This operation works on all the selected layers."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Selection as outline{"_N_
      "This converts the selection of an area into the one pixel"_N_
      "wide selection of just it's border. You may expand or shrink"_N_
      "the selection later."_N_
      "This operation works on all the selected layers."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Extrude selection{"_N_
      "You can enter an angel and a pixel distance to make the selection"_N_
      "\"3D\" thus having a feature to simply create shadows or similar."_N_
      "Maybe a good setting is 45 degrees."_N_
      "This operation works on all the selected layers."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Apply selections to layer{"_N_
      "Combine all selections from the selected layers and put them onto"_N_
      "the currently active layer."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Clear all other layer selections{"_N_
      "Invalidate all selections on the layers that aren't the current"_N_
      "active layer."_N_
    "}"_N_
  "}"_N_
  "View{"_N_
    "Gallery{"_N_
      "You can view a folders image contents as closeups with this."_N_
      "There is an option to select the folder and to skip through"_N_
      "the images. You may also use keys or the mouse to skip."_N_
      "You may also directly select the picture you mean from the"_N_
      "list."_N_
      "There is a scaling option to even view very tall pictures."_N_
      "The loading of big pictures take a while, so maybe just"_N_
      "stay patient at loading."_N_
      "You can also directly load the middle picture."_N_
      "It gets add to the pictures list and can directly be edited after"_N_
      "loading it."_N_
      "The gallery shows just the single layer/preview for a picture."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Monitor gamma{"_N_
      "Let's you enter a gamma value for the monitor."_N_
      "Gamma is actually the color value raised to the power of"_N_
      "the specified gamma value. This may help with editing non"_N_
      "linear assets. However since it's not a 1:1 mapping anymore"_N_
      "maybe the visibility of the colors is hard to distinguish for"_N_
      "certain colors."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Aspect ratio 16:9{"_N_
      "FreeDOS runs with resolution like 1024x768 (Vesa/Bios). But"_N_
      "current monitors (as of 2026) mostly use resolutions"_N_
      "like 1280x720. This option makes it possible to use the 1024x768"_N_
      "option on 1280x720 monitors."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Zoom 100%{"_N_
      "Sets the zoom factor to 1:1 mapping."_N_
      "The zooming gets applied from the center of the \"screen\""_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Zoom 200%{"_N_
      "Sets the zoom factor to 1:2 mapping."_N_
      "The zooming gets applied from the center of the \"screen\""_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Zoom in{"_N_
      "Zooms in by a small value, you can also use keys to do that"_N_
      "The zooming gets applied from the center of the \"screen\""_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Zoom out{"_N_
      "Zooms out by a small value, you can also use keys to do that"_N_
      "The zooming gets applied from the center of the \"screen\""_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Show layer shapes{"_N_
      "The layer size and position is painted as yellow rectangles also"_N_
      "to the screen."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Show grid{"_N_
      "Shows a grid. You may use some keys to snap the mouse to the grid."_N_
      "The grid can be configured in image properties (menu point)\"Image\"."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Center to view{"_N_
      "Places the current image onto the center of the \"screen\"."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Fit to view{"_N_
      "Places the current image onto the center of the \"screen\" and"_N_
      "zooms it to fit the \"screen\"."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Clear mouse lock{"_N_
      "You can lock x or y axis of the mouse in order to paint straight"_N_
      "lines. With this option here you can also remove the lock besides"_N_
      "the keys for that."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Show only selected layers selection{"_N_
      "If you disable this option the selections of all layers bleed"_N_
      "through. So to say you see all layer selections at once/combined."_N_
    "}"_N_
  "}"_N_
  "Filter{"_N_
    "Difference clouds{"_N_
      "Creates a pseudo fractal mountain scape like thing."_N_
      "You may use it several times to bring variation."_N_
      "It just modifies/changes a bit the current pictures pixels."_N_
      "The algorithm looks a bit linear so maybe some smoothing"_N_
      "or similar need to be used between difference cloud filter steps."_N_
      "The operation gets directly started after clicking the menu point."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Noise{"_N_
      "Puts values from 0..255 as grey values into the current layer."_N_
      "Maybe you can use threshholding of postprocessing or"_N_
      "gradient curves or binarysation to make the noise more your way."_N_
      "The operation gets directly started after clicking the menu point."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Edge detect{"_N_
      "Use the morphological gradient to detect edges."_N_
      "The layer is turned into some outlines."_N_
      "The operation gets directly started after clicking the menu point."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Blur{"_N_
      "Here several image blur techniques are available."_N_
      "Most notably the Gauss blur which turns the picture into a very"_N_
      "soft version of it self. For every blur type you can specify"_N_
      "the radius/size for the softening."_N_
      "Some blurs are extremely imperformant here. The Gauss blur"_N_
      "is ok from the performance perspective."_N_
      "These are the available blur types:"_N_
      "Gauss - a gaussian blur."_N_
      "Box - a \"rectangle\" blur."_N_
      "Iterative - a stepwise pixel blur."_N_
      "Radial - a directional blur with an angle and a size."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Alpha soften{"_N_
      "This blurs the alpha channel in a \"1pixel\" radius."_N_
      "So to say it makes the edges of hard shapes more soft."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Turn to glow{"_N_
      "Uses a gaussian blur to have a soft greyscale picture."_N_
      "You can specify the radius/size of the softening."_N_
      "It is a good idea to use another transparency mode like"_N_
      "\"Add\" for the layer then."_N_
      "You may use postprocessing or gradient curves to colorize"_N_
      "the glow. A good idea is to use \"Remove green\" and recolor"_N_
      "the glow via \"Hue\" in postprocessing."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Emboss{"_N_
      "This takes the luminance of each pixel and it's surrounding"_N_
      "to calculate a direction of the \"heightmap\"."_N_
      "You can use an angle to specify the 2D direction of the light."_N_
      "Maybe some blurring should be added before or after."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Color keying{"_N_
      "This maybe used to make a certain color transparent."_N_
      "There is a simple version for red,green or blue."_N_
      "And a version where the paint color is removed."_N_
      "You can specify a strength of the removal and even"_N_
      "make it binary (0 or 255) by a setting."_N_
      "It's also possible to invert the keying (0->255,255->0)."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Denoise{"_N_
      "A median filter is applied. It makes 1 or even 2 pixel sparkles"_N_
      "disappear. However the whole picture loses somehow crispiness."_N_
      "The operation gets directly started after clicking the menu point."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Sharpen{"_N_
      "The picture gets a bit more crispy by this."_N_
      "The operation gets directly started after clicking the menu point."_N_
    "}"_N_
  "}"_N_
  "Pictures{"_N_
    "Here all the currently loaded pictures are visible."_N_
    "The menupoint shows the number of loaded pictures[count]."_N_
    "You can switch the picture here and can see the active"_N_
    "picture by a checked sign."_N_
    "Delete picture{"_N_
      "Deletes the currently active picture and frees it's memory again."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Picture info{"_N_
      "This menu point only applies to pictures saved as .wyp images."_N_
      "You can enter the author of the image and add a larger"_N_
      "comment here. You can also see the timestamp of the image"_N_
      "creation which may not be the actual files timestamp."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Insert layers from other picture{"_N_
      "You can select another picture here in a dialog."_N_
      "There will be it's selected layers taken and copied to the"_N_
      "current image. The layers get inserted above the first selected"_N_
      "layer in the current image."_N_
    "}"_N_
  "}"_N_
  "Help{"_N_
    "About{"_N_
      "Just a small note on the version of the program."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Hotkeys{"_N_
      "A list of special keys to use whilst using Wypa."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "If you are new{"_N_
      "Some explanations on what's different to other paint programs."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Show tooltips{"_N_
      "If you hover a user interface item with the mouse a tiny text"_N_
      "is displayed, if this option is enabled."_N_
    "}"_N_
    "Show debug window{"_N_
      "Just some stats for debugging"_N_
      "FPS = the current frames per second of the program."_N_
      "since nothing is done via specialized graphic card instruction."_N_
      "the program may perform bad. Actually the DJGPP build"_N_
      "is much faster than a WatcomC build."_N_
      "The free memory shown is not reliable in any way. But should"_N_
      "go down, if not enough memory is available."_N_
    "}"_N_
  "}"_N_
  "Zoom{"_N_
    "Here you can update the current pictures zoom level."_N_
    "When you update this value the image get's zoomed"_N_
    "from the center of the \"screen\"."_N_
  "}"_N_
  "Mouse rate{"_N_
    "This is to control the speed of the mouse."_N_
    "Maybe you need a slower or faster pace regarding"_N_
    "your mouse movements."_N_
  "}"_N_
